# DTF tier manifest: conda-migration-indexed-timestamp  (artifact-keeper#6528)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams.mock-artifactory-conda: the
# catalog tier's mock Artifactory with one `conda` repository, into which the
# oracle copies a real noarch package. The mock reports every item as
# created 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z.
#
# THE BUG (#6528): the migration inserted conda rows at the import time, so
# every migrated package's CEP 47 `indexed_timestamp` was the import time and
# client `exclude-newer` windows held back the whole migrated channel. A
# re-import that revived a soft-deleted row kept the deleted row's time.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)     the migrated row's created_at, which a hosted channel serves as
#             indexed_timestamp, is the source's created time
#             (1767225600000); after the row is
#             soft-deleted (with an older time) and the migration re-run, the
#             revived row's created_at is the source's created time again.
#             RED on main: the import time, and the deleted row's old time.
#   (CONTROL) the migration completes with the one file into a conda
#             repository.
COVERS="6528"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-artifactory-conda"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
